BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Slow Meditative Birding Journey
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T183000
UID:260907Xss3XMbQdE6Opxsqwtivvg
DESCRIPTION:Do you enjoy a slow walk in a valley\, breezes\, wil
 dflowers\, the sounds of songbirds\, the taste of a Douglas Fir
  needle or a California Bay leaf\, the aroma of Tarweed\, or w
 atching wild turkeys and California Quail hunt for seeds and ins
 ects in the grass? Join Certified California Naturalists and Suga
 rloaf docents for this series of meandering explorations. Each mo
 nth \\(weather permitting\\) we will explore one or two of our 
 three accessible trails-- the Creekside Trail\, the Nature Trail\,
  and the Meadow trail. Suitable for all levels and a range of
  mobility\, these Sunday afternoon adventures will accommodate peo
 ple using walkers or wheelchairs\, young children\, parents with 
 babies in strollers\, as well as those who just enjoy slow walk
 s in nature that stimulate the five senses. \n\nOur October outi
 ng will focus on meditative birding. We will start off by sitti
 ng quietly for 10 minutes with Merlin app recording in 3 differ
 ent locations\, followed by about 10 minutes of discussion of th
 e birds we heard\, using Cornell to confirm their calls and son
 gs before moving onto the next sitting spot. We will also saunt
 er \\(while looking for birds\\) between the locations for a tot
 al distance of ~1.3 miles on an accessible trail. Birding by ea
 r lends itself to meditation because it works best when you sit
  silently and listening closely \\(i.e.\, if Merlin hears somethi
 ng you did not\, it reminds you that your mind has wandered\\).
  \n\nTickets are $5 for adults and free for children under 18 
 years of age. All minors must be accompanied by parent or legal
  guardian. Tickets day-of\, on site will be $10 and might not 
 be available. Meet at the White Barn parking lot.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026-ocjourn
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Haunted Wine Tour & Tasting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T173000
UID:260831qJDuR9of_Eu5Jqo_Tk5TDQ
DESCRIPTION:This fall\, Buena Vista Winery invites you to uncover the myst
 eries\, legends\, and ghostly encounters woven into more than 165 years of
  history. Led by Sonoma historian and actor George Webber\, this immersive
  90 minute experience journeys through the historic Press House and Champa
 gne Cellars\, revealing true tales of unexplained happenings reported by B
 uena Vista team members and visitors throughout the years.\n\nHear the sto
 ries of the Glowing Ghostly Shirt\, the Little Girl Who Says Hi\, the myst
 erious Ghost Party on the Second Floor\, the Old Man Who Walked Into a Sto
 ne Wall\, and other strange occurrences that continue to add to the legend
  of Buena Vista.\n\nAlong the way\, explore some of the winery’s most in
 triguing spaces\, including the Bubble Lounge\, Cave of Curiosities\, and 
 Wine Tool Museum\, while enjoying five Buena Vista wines tasted throughout
  the experience\, including a taste drawn directly from barrel.\n\nAnd\, a
 s with any journey through Buena Vista’s extraordinary past\, you never 
 quite know when the winery’s legendary founder\, Count Agoston Haraszthy
 \, may choose to make an appearance.\n\nHistory\, wine\, mystery\, and per
 haps a spirit or two await.
LOCATION:Buena Vista Historical Winery
URL:https://eventvesta.com/events/160340/t/tickets
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
