BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Meet + Greet: Bunns Rabbit II by Alan Barillaro
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261019T153000
UID:261014ndQOnf06UE2EFrO79r6QEg
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special meet-and-greet event with Alan Barillaro
 \, author of Bunns Rabbit II . This event is free\, but we appreciate your
  RSVP below so we can plan for your attendance. ABOUT THE BOOK One adventu
 re has ended\, only for a new epic journey to begin . . . Author-illustrat
 or and Academy Award–winning filmmaker Alan Barillaro takes his storytel
 ling and artwork to new heights in a compelling sequel. When Bunns Rabbit 
 returns from her quest to find the Spirit Fox\, she hopes to go back to he
 r quiet life among her family. But Fox has other plans for her. A war is o
 n the horizon\, pitting the Spirits of the Sea and Wind against those of t
 he Land and Fire. According to Fox\, only one little rabbit stands in thei
 r way—her. This time there is more than just her family on the line. It 
 is up to Bunns to save every living creature on the land before they are w
 ashed away by the sea forever. With war imminent and newly acquired powers
  she barely understands\, Bunns must avert disaster and find it within her
 self to stand up and face this new world\, whether she is ready to or not.
  With his inviting prose\, warm illustrations\, and dramatic graphic panel
 s\, Alan Barillaro brings another action- packed tale of daring\, bravery\
 , and adventure\, filled with heart\, kindness\, and hope. ABOUT THE AUTHO
 R Alan Barillaro is an acclaimed author\, illustrator\, and Academy Award-
 winning filmmaker whose work spans the worlds of picture books\, middle gr
 ade novels and animation. Born in Canada and now living in California\, he
  spent over two decades at Pixar Animation Studios\, working as a supervis
 ing animator on many popular theatrical releases\, including The Incredibl
 es\, Incredibles 2\, WALL·E\, and Brave. In 2016 he directed Piper — a 
 short film about a tiny sandpiper learning to face her fears — which won
  the Academy Award for Best Animated Short Film. Now he brings those same 
 storytelling instincts to his novels and illustrated books\, telling tende
 r\, humorous\, deeply felt stories for the small readers in all of us.
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1702350744177016/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
