BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dia de Muertos at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T170000
UID:260930U0YlkTCFzUCd6UT0WaWmVg
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of Día de Muertos\, Jack London State Historic
  Park will present two *ofrendas* in the House of Happy Walls Museum from 
 Oct. 4 to Nov. 6\, 2026.\n\nDia de Muertos\, or Day of the Dead\, is a tra
 dition that began in Mexican and other Latino cultures.  An ofrenda\, Spa
 nish for ‘offering\,’ is an altar created to honor and welcome the mem
 ory of those who have died.\n\nThe Legacy Ofrenda will honor writer and ad
 venturer Jack London\, Charmian London\, and other individuals connected t
 o the history of the property. Through photographs\, reproductions\, tradi
 tional elements of an ofrenda\, and carefully selected symbolic objects\, 
 the installation will reflect Jack and Charmian's partnership\, writing an
 d travels\, their life at Beauty Ranch\, their connection to the land\, an
 d the legacies they left behind.\n\nThe Community Ofrenda will be a shared
 \, participatory offering. Visitors\, locals\, volunteers\, Board members\
 , and employees can contribute a small photograph\, written name\, memory\
 , drawing or message honoring someone who has passed away – including a 
 beloved pet. \n\nThe installation will grow throughout October as more pe
 ople participate.  Materials will be available at the display for visitor
 s who would like to join the celebration and contribute a name\, memory or
  even a drawing of their loved one.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/dia-de-muertos-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Appetizers & Dinner Party Themes with Erin Shallat
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T113000
UID:260928EWUKM0M5hEiYfFlW0EJOEA
DESCRIPTION:Wednesday\, September 30\, 2026 10:00 am to 11:30 am\n\nWeekly
  on Wednesdays\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 109\, Rotary Kitchen\n\nCategory\n\nCul
 inary Arts\, Wellness\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nAges\n\n18 and 
 older\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$15\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nIncluded\n\nTotal 
 Registration Cost:\n\n$15\n\nAs the founder of Erin Shallat Catering in Sa
 n Francisco\, Erin brings over two decades of experience in transforming n
 utrition into an art form. Her unique approach intertwines advanced studie
 s in nutrition with a deep passion for the culinary arts. Erin’s goal is
  to make meal prep approachable and not intimidating for everyone\, encour
 aging students to gain confidence in the kitchen. She believes in working 
 with seasonal produce and what’s available\, helping students learn to c
 reate health-conscious yet tantalizing menus that embrace both flavor and 
 wellness. Introducing our Fall/Winter Cooking Series—designed for both r
 eturning and new students. This six-week program runs Mondays and Wednesda
 ys\, each with a unique focus to offer variety\, skill-building\, and fun 
 throughout the season.Wednesdays are all about creativity and fun! Each we
 ek features a new theme centered on easy appetizers and dinner party dishe
 s. From festive bites to crowd-pleasers\, these sessions will inspire stud
 ents to host gatherings or simply enjoy something new on their own.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/appetizers-dinner-party-the
 mes-with-erin-shallat/2026-09-30/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
