BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hosting 101 at Great Company
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T200000
UID:261015f9QPbSdG6Eu8mvI_hh1EJQ
DESCRIPTION:You’ve said “we should get together” a hundred times. Th
 is is the class where you actually do it.\n\nHosting isn’t about a perfe
 ct house\, matching napkins\, or a fancy menu. It’s about opening the do
 or and making people feel glad they came. Over one relaxed evening around 
 our table\, we’ll walk through the whole arc of having people over: who 
 to invite and how to ask\, how to set up so you’re not stuck in the kitc
 hen\, and what to do in those first awkward ten minutes when everyone arri
 ves.\n\nThen we’ll make dinner without turning on a stove. In small grou
 ps\, you’ll build a generous spread. Think bread\, cheese\, tinned fish\
 , pickles\, something sweet. You’ll learn how much to buy\, how to make 
 a board look abundant\, and how to make an evening come together with ease
 . Then we’ll all sit down and eat what we made.\n\nBefore you leave\, yo
 u’ll pick a date and send a real invitation. Yes\, really. We’ll help 
 you write it.\n\nYou’ll go home with a one-page hosting plan\, a shoppin
 g list you can use every time\, and a few new faces you might want to invi
 te. Food\, drinks\, and all materials included. Bring a friend with the pa
 ir ticket. No experience\, big kitchen\, or cooking skills required.
LOCATION:Great Company
URL:https://montgomeryvillageca.com/event/hosting-101-at-great-company/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Local Author/Classicist Abigail Palmer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T203000
UID:261014kOeOFif5Mk2JxlJyfLcLbQ
DESCRIPTION:St. Maximilian Catholic School (formerly Kolbe-Trinity) is hos
 ting local author/classicist\, Abigail Palmer\, at the Trinitas Cellars Ro
 om at the Meritage Resort in Napa on Thursday\, Oct. 22nd at 7:00 P.M. Pal
 mer\, the author of historical fiction novels *Faelan and the Miracle Mac
 hines* and *Faelan and the Fury of Alexandria \,* will speak on the topic
 : "*The Odyssey:* A Journey into the Epic". There is no charge for this e
 vent. Donations are gratefully accepted.
LOCATION:Trinitas Cellars Room @ The Meritage Resort and Spa
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/local-author-classicist
 -abigail-palmer/20172009/2026-10-22T19
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
