BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ocean's Unseen Frequencies by Firuze Gokce - Art Reception
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T190000
UID:2610146EEpCwNLGUKJBY71s720_Q
DESCRIPTION:I’m delighted to invite you to **“Ocean’s Unseen Frequen
 cies\,”** my new art exhibition celebrating the hidden soundscapes of th
 e ocean and the fascinating world of whale communication.\n\nThrough my ar
 twork\, I transform real whale sound spectrograms\, acoustic patterns\, an
 d scientific observations into vibrant visual expressions. My work explore
 s the connections between sound\, science\, art\, and the natural world\, 
 inviting us to experience the ocean in a different way and discover the ex
 traordinary stories hidden beneath the surface.\n\n**The event will also f
 eature a special talk by Michael Stocker**\, acoustician\, naturalist\, mu
 sician\, and founding director of Ocean Conservation Research. With decade
 s of experience in marine bioacoustics and ocean conservation\, Michael ha
 s dedicated his work to understanding how underwater noise affects marine 
 life. I’m excited to bring together art and scientific perspectives for 
 an engaging conversation about ocean sound and the importance of protectin
 g the acoustic environment of marine animals.\n\nThis exhibition is especi
 ally meaningful to me as I prepare for the next chapter of my artistic jou
 rney. I’ve been selected to participate in an **Arctic Circle Art Reside
 ncy in Svalbard**\, where I hope to explore the soundscapes of the Arctic\
 , from whale vocalizations to the cracking and shifting of sea ice\, and t
 ranslate these sounds into new works of art.\n\n**I’ll also be fundraisi
 ng at this event to help support my Arctic Circle Art Residency.** Your pr
 esence\, encouragement\, and support will help me bring this project to li
 fe and continue exploring the intersection of art\, science\, and ocean co
 nservation.\n\nI would love to see you there\, share the stories behind my
  paintings\, hear Michael’s insights\, and celebrate the incredible worl
 d of sound that connects us to our planet.\n\nThank you for being part of 
 this journey. I look forward to seeing you!
LOCATION:Keller Street Co-work
URL:https://orangeorca.art/events/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Rocky Horror Show- The Live Musical!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T200000
