DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T200000
UID:260910Whls3AGAM0yGxkfIKJId4w
DESCRIPTION:SIRSY is a ROCK & SOUL DUO with lots of pop sensibility & just
  the right amount of sass! Fronted by charismatic lead singer\, Melanie wh
 o is also the band's drummer and plays a full kit standing up. Melanie pla
 ys bass parts on a keyboard with her drum stick and even throws in some me
 an flute solos. Rich Libutti plays a road worn and well loved Rickenbacker
  through a pedal board full of vintage effects. He also pays bass with his
  feet and tells super nerdy Star Wars jokes. SIRSY is known for passionate
  performances that often include lots of stories from the road\, laughs\, 
 and dance parties. It's a good time! :\\) SIRSY plays 250\\+ shows per yea
 r nationally & has played with Grace Potter\, Maroon 5\, Cheap Trick\, Tra
 in\, and many more.  Their music is featured on Showtime’s hit tv show 
 “Shameless”. CHECK OUT SIRSY: http://www.sirsy.com VIDEO: https://www.
 youtube.com/watch?v=gx6RJZMelds
LOCATION:JaM Cellars
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108625661?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Analog Dog
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T200000
UID:260910DmTjhGlG6k-s9GLx7CEG6w
DESCRIPTION:Analog Dog makes genre fluid music in San Francisco\, USA. Hai
 ling from all corners of the country\, the band came together in and aroun
 d the hallowed musical breeding grounds of Golden Gate Park\, with the int
 ent to carry on the spirit of the legendary musical city. With each member
  drawing on diverse inspirations and musical backgrounds\, from self-taugh
 t to classically trained\, they unite over a common love for genre-bending
  composition and improvisation. Honoring the vibrations of the psychedelic
  revolution of the 1960s\, digging into the disco grooves from the dance r
 evolution of the 1970s\, and simultaneously embracing modern indie pop sou
 ndscapes\, Analog Dog is its own thing.\n\nThe release of their multi-genr
 e debut LP 'Color TV' was a landmark success for the band last year\, and 
 the same can be expected with the release of their 2nd full length LP 'IT'
 S NOT THE MONEY WE'LL REMEMBER'. With recent performances including openin
 g for The Script at the famed Fox Theater in Oakland\, a two week tour to 
 Mexico City\, summer tour dates throughout the western U.S.\, and having t
 hrown their own festivals for thousands of music fans in Golden Gate Park 
 and Jerry Garcia Amphitheater over the last few years\, the band has wille
 d their way into the hearts of Bay Area and international audiences alike.
  As they set their sights on the next step\, Analog Dog is committed to cr
 eating a vibration that reminds every audience of the magic that exists wi
 thin all of us.\n\nSan Francisco based band Analog Dog announced that thei
 r new record IT’S NOT THE MONEY WE’LL REMEMBER will be released Januar
 y 16\, 2026. The album comes after the release of six psychedelic disco fu
 sion singles which have received love from around the world. As they prepa
 re for their headline tour in support of the record\, the band is continui
 ng to demonstrate that they have something truly unique\, fresh and deep t
 o offer people.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1039650303?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Cost of Growth
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T210000
UID:2608316clH2vpuSUi4CD6A7Ck8sg
DESCRIPTION:Who owns the economy? Is infinite economic growth sustainable?
  The Cost of Growth connects local struggles against extractivism in Serbi
 a\, Italy and Sapmi with broader debates on justice\, democracy\, and war.
  It shows how people across Europe are not only resisting false solutions\
 , but also building alternatives - from grassroots organising to new forms
  of cooperation and solidarity.
LOCATION:Peace & Justice Center of Sonoma County
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/the-cost-of-growth/1978
 1220/2026-10-22T18
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
