DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T223000
UID:261015VxHfbV3-Ak2vOa5-we5H4g
DESCRIPTION:Petaluma-based Dominican singer-songwriter Edú Bega \\(new EP
  Larimar\\) and Bay Area multilingual world-pop band Razteria share a bili
 ngual night of Latin music in an intimate 75-seat room. The two artists re
 corded "En Spanglish Es Mejor" together. Razteria's music blends Latin roo
 ts with world pop\, heard on the alternative Latin album Tocar las Estrell
 as and its earth-honoring anthem "Madre Tierra." Edú also plays "Día de 
 los Mystic" on Oct 31 at the Mystic Theatre in Petaluma\, joined by Razter
 ia on support vocals.
LOCATION:The Lost Church
URL:https://thelostchurch.org/santa-rosa/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Parenting In Practice
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T150000
UID:261015Oxd08E2RGEW4gF2Azu0J3A
DESCRIPTION:Sonoma Academy will bring together parents and nationally reco
 gnized experts for Parenting in Practice\, a community-wide symposium focu
 sed on the challenges families face while raising children in an increasin
 gly complex and technology-driven world.  \n\nMark your calendars for Sat
 urday\, October 24\, for Parenting in Practice. This special day of keynot
 e speakers\, breakout sessions\, and panel discussions offers something fo
 r those at every stage of the parenting. \n\nParenting in Practice is ope
 n to the broader community\, including parents of younger children and tee
 nagers. Admission is free and includes access to all sessions. \n\nPanel 
 Details Below: \n\nWhat to Consider When Choosing a School\, featuring: 
 Percy L. Abram\, Head of School at Sonoma Academy\; Tracie Mastronicola\, 
 Head of School at The Healdsburg School\; Cecily Stock\, Head of School at
  The Presentation School\; and Brad Weaver\, Head of School at Sonoma Coun
 try Day School.\n\nHow to Succeed in College (and Life)\, on helping your 
 child to find the intersection between achievement\, fulfillment\, and joy
  featuring Dan Lerner\, NYU Professor and Author of U Thrive.\n\nJason Cra
 ige Harris\, Educator and CEO of Perception Strategies on teaching kids ab
 out agency\, boundaries\, healthy relationships\, and the responsible use 
 of power through healthy relationships and communication.\n\nLori Getz\, I
 nternet safety expert and founder of Cyber Education Consultants on keepin
 g kids safe online.\n\nDr. Devorah Heitner\, author of Growing Up in Publi
 c: Coming of Age in a Digital World and Screenwise: Helping Kids Thrive (a
 nd Survive) in Their Digital World on helping your kids manage the effects
  of social media and digital communication.
LOCATION:Sonoma Academy
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/parenting-in-practice/2
 0192748/2026-10-24T09
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
