BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Creative Photography Workshop at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T150000
UID:260930GqlBXWz1REamC3daG0kSDw
DESCRIPTION:Join professional photographers Susan and Neil Silverman\, www
 .silvermansphotography.com\, for an inspiring\, hands-on exploration of yo
 ur phone camera’s creative potential.\n\nThe first half of the class wil
 l be held in the House of Happy Walls Museum.  The instructors will demon
 strate camera settings\, creative features\, and practical techniques that
  will help you make the most of the camera you carry every day. The demons
 trations are designed to teach how the camera works and to inspire your ey
 e for composition\, light\, and storytelling.\n\nAfter a short lunch break
 \, the group will move to Beauty Ranch to photograph a variety of subjects
  while practicing the techniques just learned. Discover new photographic t
 echniques and creative possibilities while you experience and appreciate t
 he remarkable beauty\, history\, and atmosphere of Jack London State Histo
 ric Park. It’s the perfect setting to experiment\, ask questions\, and d
 evelop both technical skills creative vision.\n\nPhotographers of all expe
 rience levels are welcome\, and any smartphone camera may be used. Demonst
 rations will be presented on a newer iPhone\, but the concepts and techniq
 ues apply to virtually all modern smartphones.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/phone-photography-october-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dia de Muertos at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T170000
UID:2609308Fgst-2on0WKq0M5fjSPIg
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of Día de Muertos\, Jack London State Historic
  Park will present two *ofrendas* in the House of Happy Walls Museum from 
 Oct. 4 to Nov. 6\, 2026.\n\nDia de Muertos\, or Day of the Dead\, is a tra
 dition that began in Mexican and other Latino cultures.  An ofrenda\, Spa
 nish for ‘offering\,’ is an altar created to honor and welcome the mem
 ory of those who have died.\n\nThe Legacy Ofrenda will honor writer and ad
 venturer Jack London\, Charmian London\, and other individuals connected t
 o the history of the property. Through photographs\, reproductions\, tradi
 tional elements of an ofrenda\, and carefully selected symbolic objects\, 
 the installation will reflect Jack and Charmian's partnership\, writing an
 d travels\, their life at Beauty Ranch\, their connection to the land\, an
 d the legacies they left behind.\n\nThe Community Ofrenda will be a shared
 \, participatory offering. Visitors\, locals\, volunteers\, Board members\
 , and employees can contribute a small photograph\, written name\, memory\
 , drawing or message honoring someone who has passed away – including a 
 beloved pet. \n\nThe installation will grow throughout October as more pe
 ople participate.  Materials will be available at the display for visitor
 s who would like to join the celebration and contribute a name\, memory or
  even a drawing of their loved one.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/dia-de-muertos-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
