BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Napa $5 Folk Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T170000
UID:260930VlpRHQW-BUqVtNsvXG8qpQ
DESCRIPTION:A $5 music festival in Napa? That’s right! \n\nNot Loud Con
 certs presents the Napa $5 Folk Festival on Oct 25 from 2 - 5 pm.\n\nThis 
 is a festival like no other - 9 bands\, 3 stages\, all indoors in downtown
  Napa\, and all not too loud! Stroll between the stages hearing amazing in
 ternationally touring bands\, local favorites\, and a few surprises. Prese
 nted by Not Loud Concerts\, this event takes out all of the hassles and di
 scomfort of modern music festivals and puts the audience and musician's co
 mfort first. Best of all\, admission is only $5.\n\nThe festival is held e
 ntirely indoors in the historic Native Sons of the Gold West (on Coombs)\,
  in multiple rooms on a couple of different floors. Large bands will be fe
 atured in the grand ballroom\, acoustic-based bands will perform intimate 
 sets in the wood paneled meeting room\, and in the dance room there will b
 e folk dancing lessons and some surprise acts.\n\nIndoor bathrooms\, chair
 s to sit in\, room to dance and\, of course\, sound reinforcement that is 
 not too loud make this festival one of a kind. All of this for just $5.\n\
 nThere is lots of nearby\, free\, parking and there are elevators in the h
 all\, along with chairs in every room. The friendly folks at the Native So
 ns Hall will have drinks for sale.\n\nBuying tickets in advance is recomme
 nded (and appreciated)\, but tickets will also be for sale at the door.\n\
 nCheck out the amazing bands.\n\nDirty Cello - internationally touring blu
 egrass and blues band\n\nLaurie Lewis - one of the founders of California 
 bluegrass music\n\nFrog Face Band - Americana and bluegrass band\n\nCoyote
  Slim - traditional blues and old time folk songs with humorous stories\n\
 nCosmo and Leslie - a local bluesy folk rock duo\n\nClementine Darling - a
 n indie folk/americana musician\n\nLovejack - cellist playing Bridgerton -
  like arrangements of modern songs\n\nLindsay Everly - Americana singer-so
 ngwriter \n\nFolk dancing lessons from Marian Snyder of Berkeley Folk Dan
 ce\n\nNapa $5 Folk Festival\n\nNative Sons of the Golden West\n\n927 Coomb
 s St\, Napa\, CA 94559\n\nOct 25 from 2 - 5 pm\n\nTickets: $5 at NotLoudCo
 ncerts.com
LOCATION:Native Sons of the Golden West
URL:https://www.notloudconcerts.com/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Boo! Let’s Dance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T160000
UID:260930BrKEOXVjZkWAaiTd3G7R7g
DESCRIPTION:Boo! Let’s Dance\n\nOctober 25\, 2026\, at 3:00 pm\n\nWeill 
 Hall\, Green Music Center\n\n**Francesco Lecce-Chong**\, conductor\n\n**Ja
 co Wong**\, SRSYO conductor\n\n**North Coast Ballet California**\n\n**JOHA
 NNES BRAHMS**: Hungarian Dance \\[Ungarische Tänze\\] No. 5 in G minor fo
 r Orchestra\n\n**ARTURO MÁRQUEZ**: Dance \\[Danzón\\] No. 2 for Orchestr
 a (excerpt)\n\n**MAURICE RAVEL**: Suite from *Mother Goose* \\[*Ma mère l
 ’Oye*\\]\n\n**FLORENCE PRICE** (arr. William Grant Still): “Nimble Fee
 t” from *Dances in the Canebrakes*\n\n**JOHANN STRAUSS JR.**: *On the Be
 autiful Blue Danube* \\[*An der schönen blauen Donau*\\] (excerpt)\n\n**A
 LBERTO GINASTERA**: “Danza final” (Malambo) from *Estancia*\, op. 8a\n
 \n**Explore the World Through Music**\n\nDance\, imagine\, and explore wit
 h Snoopy and the Symphony in this lively concert celebrating musical tradi
 tions from around the world.\n\nFrom Brahms’s Hungarian Dance No. 5 to M
 árquez’s Danzón No. 2\, the program travels across cultures through mu
 sic and movement. North Coast Ballet California takes the stage for Ravel
 ’s *Mother Goose*\, while Snoopy adds to the fun in an interactive perfo
 rmance that will have the whole family moving to the music!\n\n*Costumes a
 re encouraged.*\n\n© Peanuts Worldwide LLC\n\n**Programs\, artists\, date
 s\, and prices are subject to change without notice. Tickets are subject t
 o availability. All Tickets are nonrefundable.**
LOCATION:Green Music Center
URL:https://www.srsymphony.org/event/boo-lets-dance/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dia de Muertos at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T170000
UID:2609307Syc5DZdT0yS2eo2WE4adA
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of Día de Muertos\, Jack London State Historic
  Park will present two *ofrendas* in the House of Happy Walls Museum from 
 Oct. 4 to Nov. 6\, 2026.\n\nDia de Muertos\, or Day of the Dead\, is a tra
 dition that began in Mexican and other Latino cultures.  An ofrenda\, Spa
 nish for ‘offering\,’ is an altar created to honor and welcome the mem
 ory of those who have died.\n\nThe Legacy Ofrenda will honor writer and ad
 venturer Jack London\, Charmian London\, and other individuals connected t
 o the history of the property. Through photographs\, reproductions\, tradi
 tional elements of an ofrenda\, and carefully selected symbolic objects\, 
 the installation will reflect Jack and Charmian's partnership\, writing an
 d travels\, their life at Beauty Ranch\, their connection to the land\, an
 d the legacies they left behind.\n\nThe Community Ofrenda will be a shared
 \, participatory offering. Visitors\, locals\, volunteers\, Board members\
 , and employees can contribute a small photograph\, written name\, memory\
 , drawing or message honoring someone who has passed away – including a 
 beloved pet. \n\nThe installation will grow throughout October as more pe
 ople participate.  Materials will be available at the display for visitor
 s who would like to join the celebration and contribute a name\, memory or
  even a drawing of their loved one.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/dia-de-muertos-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
