BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sweeney Todd
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T140000
UID:260909arneTBDJlE6ea0tHx-A2ww
DESCRIPTION:Sweeney Todd is largely considered one of Stephen Sondheim’s
  masterpieces. With it\, he aimed to create a musical that could “scare 
 the hell out of everyone\,” and yet\, somehow\, be funny.\n\nThe story c
 enters around Sweeney Todd\, an unjustly exiled barber who returns to Lond
 on\, seeking vengeance against the lecherous judge who framed him and rava
 ged his young wife. The road to revenge leads Todd to Mrs. Lovett\, a reso
 urceful proprietress of a failing pie shop\, above which\, he opens a new 
 barber practice. Mrs. Lovett’s luck sharply shifts when Todd’s thirst 
 for blood inspires the integration of an ingredient into her meat pies tha
 t has the people of 19th Century London lining up…and the carnage has on
 ly just begun!\n\n\\***Content Advisory:** Adult language and violent the
 mes\, as well as controversial pie recipes. Recommended for 12+.\n\nRunnin
 g Time: 2 hours\, 40 minutes including one intermission.\n\nOctober 23rd\,
  24th\, 25th\, \\*29th\, 30th\, 31st\, Nov 1st\, 6th\, 7th\, 8th.\n\nBook 
 by Hugh Wheeler\n\nMusic and Lyrics by Stephen Sondheim\n\nDirected by Ste
 ven David Martin\n\n**Friday and Saturday Shows:** 7:30 PM\n\n**Sunday Mat
 inee:** 2:00 PM\n\n**\\*Value Thursday:** 7:30 PM\n\n**Admission:** \n\nA
 dults: $44\n\nStudent w/ID: $10\n\n\\*Special Value Thursday Performanc
 e: Pay What You Can
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/sweeney-todd/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Haunted Wine Tour & Tasting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T173000
UID:260831jFbe_kUeN0ShpQmBOG9pMw
DESCRIPTION:This fall\, Buena Vista Winery invites you to uncover the myst
 eries\, legends\, and ghostly encounters woven into more than 165 years of
  history. Led by Sonoma historian and actor George Webber\, this immersive
  90 minute experience journeys through the historic Press House and Champa
 gne Cellars\, revealing true tales of unexplained happenings reported by B
 uena Vista team members and visitors throughout the years.\n\nHear the sto
 ries of the Glowing Ghostly Shirt\, the Little Girl Who Says Hi\, the myst
 erious Ghost Party on the Second Floor\, the Old Man Who Walked Into a Sto
 ne Wall\, and other strange occurrences that continue to add to the legend
  of Buena Vista.\n\nAlong the way\, explore some of the winery’s most in
 triguing spaces\, including the Bubble Lounge\, Cave of Curiosities\, and 
 Wine Tool Museum\, while enjoying five Buena Vista wines tasted throughout
  the experience\, including a taste drawn directly from barrel.\n\nAnd\, a
 s with any journey through Buena Vista’s extraordinary past\, you never 
 quite know when the winery’s legendary founder\, Count Agoston Haraszthy
 \, may choose to make an appearance.\n\nHistory\, wine\, mystery\, and per
 haps a spirit or two await.
LOCATION:Buena Vista Historical Winery
URL:https://eventvesta.com/events/160340/t/tickets
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
