BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Collectors Lunch Pairing at Lynmar Estate
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T143000
UID:2606261HdSnGSsiUufpN40QaKzMw
DESCRIPTION:Rooted in the bounty of Quail Hill Vineyard\, Lynmar Estate’
 s Summer Collectors Lunch Pairing invites guests to experience the flavors
  of Sonoma County at their seasonal peak. The elevated four-course menu sh
 owcases ingredients harvested from Lynmar’s organically farmed gardens\,
  orchards\, and olive groves. Each course is individually plated and thoug
 htfully paired with Lynmar’s acclaimed estate-grown Pinot Noirs\, Chardo
 nnays\, and sparkling wines\, creating a journey that is both deeply conne
 cted to Sonoma County and globally inspired. Served in the idyllic setting
  of Quail Hill Vineyard\, the experience is further enhanced by a special 
 tableside visit from Estate Chef David Frakes.\n\nCollectors Lunch Pairing
  Menu Summer 2026:\n\nAdam’s Vineyard Chardonnay\, 2022\n\nWarm Organic 
 Popcorn\n\n*White Corn-Kasundi Salt\, Estate Extra-Virgin Olive Oil*\n\nSu
 sanna’s Vineyard Chardonnay\, 2022\n\nThai Green Curry & Coconut Soup\n\
 n*Bliss Snap Peas & Heirloom Radish*\n\nYoung Vines Pinot Noir\, 2021\n\nH
 eirloom Potato & Cherry Tomato ‘Croustade’\n\n*Smoked Bacon-Grain Must
 ard Dressing*\n\nSusanna’s Vineyard Pinot Noir\, 2022\n\nRoasted Syrian 
 Seven-Spiced Chicken Breast\n\n*Indonesian Corn Fritter\, Summer Vegetable
  Ragout\, Balado Sauce*\n\nRosé de Blancs Sparkling\, 2021\n\nChilled Van
 illa Burnt Basque Cheesecake\n\n*Raspberry-Rose Syrup\, Black Tea & Licori
 ce-Poached Cherries*\n\n*Brown Butter Nilla Cookie\, Candied Lime*\n\n**Es
 tate Ingredients:**\n\nBay Laurel\, Cherries\, Chives\, Edible Flowers\, L
 emons\, Olive Oil\, Peas\, Potatoes\, Radishes\, Raspberries\, Thyme\, Tom
 atoes\, Zucchini and more!\n\nMenu by Estate Chef David Frakes\n\nReservat
 ions are required. Maximum group size is six guests.
LOCATION:Lynmar Estate 
URL:https://lynmarestate.com/reservation/type/collectors-lunch-pairing/ 
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seaweed Foraging on the Sonoma Coast
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T190000
UID:260528H5bkZKxToEG21-5EfpOh0A
DESCRIPTION:This 2.5 hour guided morning foray will meet on the Sonoma Coa
 st\, and be followed by a talk on what you collected\, the ecology of seaw
 eed\, and how to cook your harvest. You can expect to collect up to 10 lbs
 . of raw edible seaweed. This is a coastal forage during low tide. You won
 't need to get in the ocean\, but we recommend wearing rain boots. Please 
 note this event is for ages 9 and up. An educational hands-on workshop · 
  Learn a new food skill ·  Explore the normally-underwater inter tidal 
 zone at a negative low tide ·  Connect with your local food system ·  
 Enjoy nutritional-rich umami direct from the source.
LOCATION:Bodega Bay
URL:https://www.foragesf.com/seaweed-foraging-sonoma
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
