BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Marc Cary Trio
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T210000
UID:260715b8gYJz-L2EagC3BUsv5gFA
DESCRIPTION:In a jazz world brimming with brilliant and adventurous pianis
 ts\, Marc Cary stands apart by way of pedigree and design as one of New Yo
 rk's best jazz pianists. With his Focus Trio\, Cary strikes an organic bal
 ance between jazz harmonies and rhythms from Africa and India. Drummer and
  tabla player Sameer Gupta plays an essential role in these rhythms along 
 with bassist David Ewell\, who are the original members of the Focus Trio 
 and collaborators for over 20 years. Grammy-nominated pianist Cary brings 
 into sharp focus his many influences-from deep indigenous world rhythms to
  hard bop to classical lyricism. The energy and the cultural wealth of Har
 lem\, New York resonate in their music. Cary is alternately percussive and
  subtle\, animated and introspective\, balancing energy and lyricism with 
 a depth of personal expression that which he calls "classical indigenous j
 azz for the people." Cary's mission statement for Focus is "to bring indig
 enous rhythms together with American jazz to create new palettes of sound.
 "
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/marc-cary-trio/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
