BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dia de Muertos at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T170000
UID:260930BP-KZ0pSl0-SiK5K86m3ow
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of Día de Muertos\, Jack London State Historic
  Park will present two *ofrendas* in the House of Happy Walls Museum from 
 Oct. 4 to Nov. 6\, 2026.\n\nDia de Muertos\, or Day of the Dead\, is a tra
 dition that began in Mexican and other Latino cultures.  An ofrenda\, Spa
 nish for ‘offering\,’ is an altar created to honor and welcome the mem
 ory of those who have died.\n\nThe Legacy Ofrenda will honor writer and ad
 venturer Jack London\, Charmian London\, and other individuals connected t
 o the history of the property. Through photographs\, reproductions\, tradi
 tional elements of an ofrenda\, and carefully selected symbolic objects\, 
 the installation will reflect Jack and Charmian's partnership\, writing an
 d travels\, their life at Beauty Ranch\, their connection to the land\, an
 d the legacies they left behind.\n\nThe Community Ofrenda will be a shared
 \, participatory offering. Visitors\, locals\, volunteers\, Board members\
 , and employees can contribute a small photograph\, written name\, memory\
 , drawing or message honoring someone who has passed away – including a 
 beloved pet. \n\nThe installation will grow throughout October as more pe
 ople participate.  Materials will be available at the display for visitor
 s who would like to join the celebration and contribute a name\, memory or
  even a drawing of their loved one.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/dia-de-muertos-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Independent Projects with Amy Hamley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T210000
UID:260926-gq-OSUz9E2B4Ds7-JCH3g
DESCRIPTION:Every Tuesday · 6 Weeks\n\nDate & Time\n\nOctober 6 – Novem
 ber 10th\, 2026\n\n6:00 PM – 9:00 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 117\, Ceramics 
 Studio\n\nCategory\n\nCeramics\, Extended Classes\n\nExperience Level\n\nI
 ntermediate\n\nAges\n\n17\\+\n\nRegistration Fee:\n\n$200\n\nMaterials Fee
 :\n\n$30\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$230\n\nThis is a 6 week session w
 ith instructor\, Amy Hamley. This course is for students interested in exp
 loring both wheel throwing AND handbuilding\, and the combination of both 
 in one class! Learn from Hamley’s years of expertise in the field and en
 joy creating handbuilt\, thrown\, and altered forms. Amy caters each sylla
 bus closely to her group of students\, ensuring that every project fits th
 e desires of participants. This course encourages folks to work on indepen
 dent projects in the class\, receiving one on one support from Amy through
 out the time. This course will include demos\, exercises\, and utilize a v
 ariety of methods to achieve the desired goal for each student. Some proje
 cts may include wheel thrown vases with altered adornments\, best practice
 s for slump and hump molds\, and more.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/independent-projects-august
 /
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Raw & Rogue
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T210000
UID:260912coUzCd6duEW9AHBL9A2b-Q
DESCRIPTION:For three Tuesdays this fall\, Raw \\+ Rogue brings an intimat
 e twelve-seat omakase experience to the rooftop of Appellation Healdsburg.
  Across twelve courses\, Chef Willer Larreal Perez—a Venezuela-born chef
  trained at omakase counters in Los Angeles and Miami—builds each dish a
 round the fish\, taking guests on a scenic culinary journey from the count
 er to the plate. An amuse opens the experience and dessert brings it to a 
 close\, while wine pairings from Baron Ziegler\, co-founder of Healdsburg
 ’s Banshee Wines and founder of Marine Layer\, move alongside the menu. 
 Each course is paired with its own song\, creating a soundtrack that build
 s plate by plate as the light shifts over Northern Sonoma County. Together
 \, the food\, wine and music create a multisensory evening designed to unf
 old in rhythm with the rooftop setting. \n\nWhen: Tuesdays | September 29
 \, October 13\, October 27 \\(6:30 pm\\) \n\nPrice: $295 per guest\, wine
  selections prices separately \n\nReservations are available through Open
 Table: Raw & Rogue \n\nPre-paid reservations are required.
LOCATION:Appellation Healdsburg
URL:https://beelinerooftop.getbento.com/event/raw-rogue/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Liam St. John & Bridge City Sinners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261027T190000
UID:260910WluCVIlB70q_hL2z-aJphA
DESCRIPTION:Liam’s debut full-length project\, “stripped back” \\(Ju
 ne 2022\\) reached \\#1 in Top Blues Albums globally on Apple Music\, foll
 owed up by a successful nationwide tour that wrapped with a sold out show 
 in Music City\, USA. \n\nAt the crossroads of the blues and rock & roll\, 
 Liam St. John commands his truest form by combining lyrics that embody the
  blues with their piercing and painful truth\, and delivering a captivatin
 g performance with vibrancy true to the spirit of rock and roll. Liam floo
 ds the room with an electrifying energy\, washing over every stage he grac
 es. \n\nSt. John made his mark in Nashville after inking with King Pen Mus
 ic by way of Warner Chappell at the end of 2022. This is the blues-crooner
 ’s first publishing deal.  “I was knocked out by Liam‘s voice when I
  first heard it.  He is such a creative and unique artist with a vision li
 ke no other. His music brings a fresh new look on blues and rock in this w
 orld”\n\nLiam credits his foundation for singing to the legends he grew 
 up listening to. From Ray Charles to Etta James\, Sam Cooke\, Louis Armstr
 ong\, and Tracy Chapman\, the raw\, gritty\, blues-infused soul always sur
 faces in Liam’s songs and performances. \n\nLiam is managed by Aidan Cro
 wley with Legacy Content. //
LOCATION:Mystic Theatre & Music Hall
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108686729?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
