BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Callie Watts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T180000
UID:261011iaH21O7QmEWmjzTDDaKpoQ
DESCRIPTION:Callie Watts is a singer/songwriter from Northern California w
 ho was raised on classical music\, The Beatles and The Beach Boys before d
 iscovering Joni Mitchell\, Elton John\, Stevie Wonder\, Paul Simon\, Billy
  Joel\, Carole King\, and all the great writers of the ’60s and 70’s w
 ho have influenced her sound and writing style. After graduating high scho
 ol\, Callie began playing and performing solo\, as well as in local and ba
 y area bands of different genres. She’s played blues with Eric Lindell a
 nd the Reds\, funky soul with Phatty\, and jazz/swing with Savoy Swingers 
 along with many other various projects. Callie has taken turns throughout 
 her career as a keyboardist\, guitarist\, writer\, and lead/backing vocali
 st\, and she’s currently a member of the dynamic Sonoma County funk rock
  band Burrows and Dilbeck\, having joined in 2010 as part of the former ba
 nd Frobeck. Over time\, she’s had the honor of opening for acts such as 
 Bootsy Collins\, Elvin Bishop\, Huey Lewis and The News\, War\, Ozomatli\,
  Bill Champlin\, Booker T\, and the B52s. Callie continues to perform freq
 uently as an acoustic solo artist\, focusing on developing a core audience
  and a buzz for her original material. Come hang out and listen at venues 
 such as Aroma Roasters\, Rincon Valley Tap Room and Bottle Shop\, and Hopm
 onk Tavern.
LOCATION:Hotel Healdsburg
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108897113?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dia de Muertos at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T170000
UID:260930i6986jb5Z0y4tRXz3NjQwA
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of Día de Muertos\, Jack London State Historic
  Park will present two *ofrendas* in the House of Happy Walls Museum from 
 Oct. 4 to Nov. 6\, 2026.\n\nDia de Muertos\, or Day of the Dead\, is a tra
 dition that began in Mexican and other Latino cultures.  An ofrenda\, Spa
 nish for ‘offering\,’ is an altar created to honor and welcome the mem
 ory of those who have died.\n\nThe Legacy Ofrenda will honor writer and ad
 venturer Jack London\, Charmian London\, and other individuals connected t
 o the history of the property. Through photographs\, reproductions\, tradi
 tional elements of an ofrenda\, and carefully selected symbolic objects\, 
 the installation will reflect Jack and Charmian's partnership\, writing an
 d travels\, their life at Beauty Ranch\, their connection to the land\, an
 d the legacies they left behind.\n\nThe Community Ofrenda will be a shared
 \, participatory offering. Visitors\, locals\, volunteers\, Board members\
 , and employees can contribute a small photograph\, written name\, memory\
 , drawing or message honoring someone who has passed away – including a 
 beloved pet. \n\nThe installation will grow throughout October as more pe
 ople participate.  Materials will be available at the display for visitor
 s who would like to join the celebration and contribute a name\, memory or
  even a drawing of their loved one.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/dia-de-muertos-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
