DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T200000
UID:260910RGhNPklwMECVV9HvpH278g
DESCRIPTION:Andrew Duhon is a songwriter who's weighted\, soulful songs fe
 el like a trustworthy dispatch from the heart of his New Orleans home out 
 to the familiar landmarks of Americana Music.  No Depression call's Duhon 
 "A soulmate of Van Morrison lyrically and vocally."  He tours most commonl
 y as a trio with upright bass and drums.  4 records out thus far\, his 201
 3 album\, "The Moorings\," was nominated for a Grammy\, and he's due to re
 lease a new album in 2024.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108513219?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sweeney Todd
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T193000
UID:260909zlkUesSSeEivqw84sCanOA
DESCRIPTION:Sweeney Todd is largely considered one of Stephen Sondheim’s
  masterpieces. With it\, he aimed to create a musical that could “scare 
 the hell out of everyone\,” and yet\, somehow\, be funny.\n\nThe story c
 enters around Sweeney Todd\, an unjustly exiled barber who returns to Lond
 on\, seeking vengeance against the lecherous judge who framed him and rava
 ged his young wife. The road to revenge leads Todd to Mrs. Lovett\, a reso
 urceful proprietress of a failing pie shop\, above which\, he opens a new 
 barber practice. Mrs. Lovett’s luck sharply shifts when Todd’s thirst 
 for blood inspires the integration of an ingredient into her meat pies tha
 t has the people of 19th Century London lining up…and the carnage has on
 ly just begun!\n\n\\***Content Advisory:** Adult language and violent the
 mes\, as well as controversial pie recipes. Recommended for 12+.\n\nRunnin
 g Time: 2 hours\, 40 minutes including one intermission.\n\nOctober 23rd\,
  24th\, 25th\, \\*29th\, 30th\, 31st\, Nov 1st\, 6th\, 7th\, 8th.\n\nBook 
 by Hugh Wheeler\n\nMusic and Lyrics by Stephen Sondheim\n\nDirected by Ste
 ven David Martin\n\n**Friday and Saturday Shows:** 7:30 PM\n\n**Sunday Mat
 inee:** 2:00 PM\n\n**\\*Value Thursday:** 7:30 PM\n\n**Admission:** \n\nA
 dults: $44\n\nStudent w/ID: $10\n\n\\*Special Value Thursday Performanc
 e: Pay What You Can
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/sweeney-todd/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
