BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Back pOrchEstra's American Roots at RanchoNicasio\, CA Nov 1\, Sun
 \, 4:00-6:30
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T181500
UID:261012bsKtdSKI50yU2iVzIvETog
DESCRIPTION:Back pOrchEstra's American Roots show continues! ...at Rancho 
 Nicasio\, Nicasio\, CA November 1\, Sun\, 4:00-6:30 INDOORS- by the BEST D
 ANCE FLOOR in the North Bay.\n\nIf you don't believe me.. come try it out!
 .. Or.. if you haven't seen the band lately I urge you to come join us... 
 these folks are inspiring!\n\nChoose your Music Service!:\n\nThe album is 
 out: https://orcd.co/5xga7nr\n\n..and the Latest single\, "What Does Your 
 Heart Say?" https://orcd.co/7jjvmmx\n\nLPs\, CDs available all over\, incl
 uding https://www.globerecords.com\n\n1 Old Rancheria Rd Nicasio CA 94946 
 (415) 662-2219\n\n(Free Show\, but reservations recommended)\n\nhttps://ci
 .ovationtix.com/35892/production/1290853?performanceId=11867090\n\n$15 don
 ation suggested\n\n... w/ Candy Girard\, Tim Eschliman\, Luis Rodriguez\, 
 Jen Rund and Mark Larson! ...on resonator guitar\, violin\, bass\, telecas
 ter & traps... come on come on!\n\nwe're back on the RootsMuscReport chart
 s (#29 this week): https://www.rootsmusicreport.com/charts/view/album/sub\
 \_genre/americana-country/weekly/2026-10-03\n\n\\*recent quotes:\n\n"The g
 uitars slam like saloon doors\, the violin traces lines that oscillate bet
 ween melancholy and jubilation\, the rhythm section moves forward with a t
 ranquil groove that never rushes but never falters... Back pOrchEstra deli
 vers a luminous\, earthy\, profoundly human record. An album that makes yo
 u want to sit on a porch\, watch the sunset\, and let the stories do their
  work...." - Fred Delforge\, Zicazine\n\n"...What sets 'Stories In The Hea
 rt' apart is its sense of balance. Resonator guitar\, violin\, bass\, drum
 s\, percussion\, dobro\, and Telecaster create a flexible\, roots-forward 
 palette that allows Back Porchestra to move between styles fluidly. The so
 ngs echo traditions without reenacting them\, keeping one foot in the past
  and the other firmly planted in the present." - Vince's Hot Picks (Best o
 f 2026) New Releases Now\n\nBack pOrchEstra is a compact Shelter-in-Place-
 inspired musical combo ....going back to the basics... Formed for the firs
 t time the locked-down summer of 2020. The band draws from new original ma
 terial as well as reworked classics by Hank Williams\, Taj Mahal\, Dan Hic
 ks\, Big Bill Broonzy\, Bob Wills\, Bobby Charles ...even Christmas Jug Ba
 nd tunes\n\n... check out the "Dusty Road I'm On" video: https://youtu.be/
 jj0IIkUyrE4 ...a twangy roots rock number with a Cajun flavor and hints of
  Jesse Ed Davis and Sid Page....\n\nThe previous single\, the Neo-Motown/L
 evon Helm style "Ever Think About It\," is here: https://orcd.co/qo5579q\n
 \n"...evokes artists from multiple decades over the last century and embra
 ces everything from indie-rock and Americana to Celtic\, Motown\, and West
 ern swing. If you need a reference point\, look to bands like Dan Hicks an
 d His Hot Licks and Asleep at the Wheel\, whose records also draw on dispa
 rate sources." - Jeff Burger\, Americana Highway\n\nmore at... https://www
 .BackpOrchEstra.com\n\nBandCamp: https://backporchestra.bandcamp.com\n\nyo
 uTube: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLOTwG2XEiO2O8c0dEI-7hlpI8nr7
 apiNf\n\nBluesky: https://bsky.app/profile/backporchestra.bsky.social\n\nR
 everb Nation: https://www.reverbnation.com/backporchestra\n\nFacebook: htt
 ps://www.facebook.com/BackPorchEstra/\n\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.
 com/backporchestra/\n\n#rootsrock\n\n#americanrootsmusic\n\n#americanamusi
 c\n\n#rockabillymusic\n\n#twangyguitar\n\n#backporchestra\n\n#acousticmusi
 c\n\n#adultalbumalternative\n\n#singersongwriter\n\n#folkmusic\n\n#folkroc
 k
LOCATION:Rancho Nicasio
URL:https://www.BackpOrchEstra.com/shows.html
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Day of the Dead with the Herd: Ancestors\, Horses & the Healing of
  Grief
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T153000
UID:2610109Lix2I4VT02NmCOTmMDF8w
DESCRIPTION:Day of the Dead with the Herd: Ancestors\, Horses & the Healin
 g of Grief\n\nJoin Alane Freund\, LMFT\, and the Heart & Mind Equine herd 
 for an intimate daylong retreat honoring our ancestors\, remembering loved
  ones\, and exploring grief and healing. Inspired by Día de los Muertos a
 nd seasonal traditions of remembrance\, this unique experience combines eq
 uine-assisted therapy\, somatic practices\, sound healing\, and ritual. Pa
 rticipants are invited to bring a meaningful object for a communal ancesto
 r altar. No horse experience necessary. Lunch and refreshments included. L
 imited to 15 participants.\n\nSunday\, November 1 | 9:30 AM–3:30 PM Wood
 acre\, CA\n\nRegistration: https://www.heartmindequine.com/day-of-the-dead
LOCATION:Heart and Mind Equine
URL:https://www.heartmindequine.com/day-of-the-dead
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
