SUMMARY:Dia de los Muertos Celebration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T190000
UID:261003scUHPOCqEkeviN1hXPPCgg
DESCRIPTION:**Join us on November 1st for a magical**\n\n**Día de Los Mue
 rtos Celebration**\n\n**Bring your family and friends as we honor our love
 d ones and immerse ourselves in this beautiful tradition.**\n\n*Sugar Skul
 l Decorating & Themed Art Project Face Painting* *Traditional Mexican Food
  & Refreshing Drinks Quetzalén Dance Presentation (Ballet Folklórico)*\n
 \nThis is a family-friendly occasion open to all ages!\n\nEnjoy delicious 
 tamales and a variety of delicious Agua Fresca made by Cielito\, desserts\
 , and the traditional Pan de Muerto.\n\n**Quetzalén Folklórico begins at
  5:00 PM**\n\nFestivities will take place inside and on our outdoor patio.
LOCATION:Art Escape Sonoma
URL:https://www.artescapesonoma.com/dia-de-los-muertos-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Focaccia + Wine
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T140000
UID:261002Ur5tslRaok6ySl_oBj6Trw
DESCRIPTION:Kinda like brunch\, but better.\n\nJoin us for a relaxed after
 noon of fresh focaccia\, Adruni wine\, vineyard views\, and a little creat
 ivity around the table.\n\nWe’ll welcome you to Adruni Vineyards with a 
 glass of their **inaugural sparkling wine release** and sweeping views o
 f Dry Creek Valley. From there\, find your seat and settle in—this isn't
  your traditional cooking class.\n\nBreanna of Riverbend Farm Stand will h
 ave the sourdough prepared and ready for you to get straight to the fun pa
 rt. She’ll show you how to stretch and dimple your dough before you make
  your way through a beautiful\, seasonal topping bar to create a focaccia 
 entirely your own.\n\nThere’s no long sourdough lesson or pressure to ge
 t it perfect. Breanna will be alongside you to guide\, answer questions\, 
 and handle the baking while you sip\, create\, and enjoy the afternoon.\n\
 nOnce the focaccia goes into the oven\, we’ll gather back around the tab
 le for a taste of Adruni wines and light accompaniments while everything b
 akes.\n\nAnd you won't leave empty-handed.\n\nYour freshly baked focaccia 
 is yours to take home\, along with a Riverbend Farm Stand sourdough starte
 r and care guide so you can try your hand at it again in your own kitchen.
 \n\nCome with a friend or come on your own. Either way\, we'll save you a 
 seat at the table.\n\n**Sunday\, November 1** Adruni Vineyards | Dry Creek
  Valley **$145 per person** Limited to just **12 guests**\n\nAdditional A
 druni wines will be available for purchase during the afternoon.
LOCATION:Adruni Vineyards
URL:https://www.eventbrite.com/e/focaccia-wine-tickets-2002485607357?aff=e
 bdssbdestsearch
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dia de Muertos at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T170000
UID:2609305J0DUgHntkq2FWtKadipiA
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of Día de Muertos\, Jack London State Historic
  Park will present two *ofrendas* in the House of Happy Walls Museum from 
 Oct. 4 to Nov. 6\, 2026.\n\nDia de Muertos\, or Day of the Dead\, is a tra
 dition that began in Mexican and other Latino cultures.  An ofrenda\, Spa
 nish for ‘offering\,’ is an altar created to honor and welcome the mem
 ory of those who have died.\n\nThe Legacy Ofrenda will honor writer and ad
 venturer Jack London\, Charmian London\, and other individuals connected t
 o the history of the property. Through photographs\, reproductions\, tradi
 tional elements of an ofrenda\, and carefully selected symbolic objects\, 
 the installation will reflect Jack and Charmian's partnership\, writing an
 d travels\, their life at Beauty Ranch\, their connection to the land\, an
 d the legacies they left behind.\n\nThe Community Ofrenda will be a shared
 \, participatory offering. Visitors\, locals\, volunteers\, Board members\
 , and employees can contribute a small photograph\, written name\, memory\
 , drawing or message honoring someone who has passed away – including a 
 beloved pet. \n\nThe installation will grow throughout October as more pe
 ople participate.  Materials will be available at the display for visitor
 s who would like to join the celebration and contribute a name\, memory or
  even a drawing of their loved one.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/dia-de-muertos-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Adding Beauty and Interest to Your Garden with California Native P
 lants
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261101T130000
UID:2609304wSvkH_xhEWql8QRpNC91A
DESCRIPTION:There are many wonderful California native shrubs and perennia
 ls that make perfect additions to existing gardens and are great replaceme
 nts for non-native plants. And because they are native to this climate\, t
 hey are better able to withstand the swings in rainfall and temperature we
  are seeing more frequently.\n\nMaster Gardener Linda King will discuss so
 me reasons for adding California native plants to your garden\, and recomm
 end a variety of native plants that are easy to care for and make great ad
 ditions to any existing garden. Join us under the shade of the trees at Pe
 taluma Bounty Unity Garden. There will be a period for answering all your 
 questions.
LOCATION:Petaluma Bounty
URL:https://ucanr.edu/site/mg-sonoma
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
