BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Michelle Lambert
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T200000
UID:261012TL_aaXk1WkqHHwxAEUiu-Q
DESCRIPTION:Join Michelle at JaM Cellars in downtown Napa for an evening s
 how. More info available here: https://jamcellars.com/\n\nBay Area breakou
 t artist Michelle Lambert delivers a fun\, high-energy show filled with ed
 gy\, heartfelt original music\, infectious pop hooks\, and unstoppable cha
 risma. Fresh off a successful 40-date tour across the Western states last 
 year\, Michelle captivates audiences with soaring vocals\, dynamic violin 
 solos\, and vibrant energy that radiates through the crowd. Her electrifyi
 ng performances create an unforgettable live experience that will have you
  dancing\, smiling\, and celebrating all night long.\n\nRaised in Northern
  California and trained at the prestigious Berklee College of Music\, Mich
 elle Lambert has forged her own path as a fearless\, independent pop artis
 t. She has topped the charts of Indie Radio with her original songs and wa
 s featured in the San Francisco Giants’ City Connect Campaign as a notab
 le Bay Area artist. Michelle cut her teeth performing and writing in the c
 ompetitive music scenes of Nashville and Los Angeles before returning to t
 he Bay Area to tour with her own thriving career. Known for her powerful v
 ocals\, masterful violin playing\, and bold\, colorful costumes\, Michelle
  pairs striking visuals with raw emotional storytelling—embodying creati
 vity\, resilience\, and the adventure of chasing your dreams. For more inf
 o on Michelle visit: https://www.michellelambert.com
LOCATION:JaM Cellars
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108834608?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yellowman
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T203000
UID:261012-ocMv-SgJkiuUPgtP-NzKA
DESCRIPTION:King Yellowman has an incredible history in Reggae music. His 
 upbringing at the Maxfield Home orphanage in Kingston and being albino in 
 Jamaica were two obstacles the he overcame and went on to be \\(at one tim
 e\\) the biggest reggae artist since Bob Marley. \n\nAfter winning a talen
 t contest at Tastee Patties in Kingston\, Yellow went on to excite reggae 
 crowds all over Jamaica and the rest of the world with his boastful and so
 metimes bodacious lyrics. His ability to ride rhythm and excite a crowd ma
 de Yellow an instant hit in Jamaica. He also began to work with the Ace So
 und System in St. Thomas and drew big crowds at his dancehall performances
 . Later in his career\, Yellow began to spread out and work for a number o
 f different producers\, sometimes releasing as many as five albums per yea
 r. This led to a recording contract with CBS Records. Yellowman recorded o
 ne album with them before he was diagnosed with jaw cancer and was given s
 ix months to live. This was in 1986. After surgery an extended leave of ab
 sence from the record industry\, Yellowman began his comeback with the son
 g "Blueberry Hill"\, and his career was re-launched. His first album for R
 AS came from producer Phillip 'Fatis' Burrell and was called "Yellow Like 
 Cheese". Coincidentally this was the start of a long and fruitful relation
 ship with RAS and Yellowman and also RAS and 'Fatis' and his exterminator 
 production. Yellowman has always been very professional to work with and a
 lways a respectful and reliable human being. He has managed to outlive his
  predicted fate of death and his performances are incredibly lively as he 
 seems to have an unlimited amount of stage energy. We can only hope for th
 e best for Yellowman. He has continued his hard work and his devotion to h
 is family is to be complimented. \n\nThe rudest Dancehall toaster of the 1
 980s\, Jamaica's albino son Yellowman made as many enemies as fans with hi
 s controversial\, often overtly sexist \\(if tongue in cheek\\) lyrics. No
 w back on the Ragga scene\, singing at a slightly slower pace\, Yellowman'
 s witticisms are as cheeky\, spirited and intelligent as ever\, and delive
 red with his customary sharp\, melodic style.
LOCATION:Mystic Theatre
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1040513268?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cuban Salsa Beginner - 4-Week Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T203000
UID:261003iWcPMQGNqUKgLYKCLZjCKQ
DESCRIPTION:Cuban Salsa Class with Eric Celestino & Abigail Celestino\n\n4
 week class\n\nNovember 5- November 26\n\nClass requires a minimum of 8 reg
 istrations to run. Please register soon so we can secure the session!\n\nT
 his is a beginner cuban salsa—you will learn your basic footwork and tur
 ns.\n\nIn this class\, you will learn the fundamentals of Cuban Salsa\, in
 cluding body movement\, rhythm\, musicality\, footwork\, partner connectio
 n\, and partnerwork patterns inspired by authentic Cuban dance culture. We
  focus on proper technique\, coordination\, flow\, and natural body expres
 sion\, while also building confidence and strong foundations.\n\nClasses a
 re structured with:\n\n• Warm-up and body movement\n\n• Footwork and r
 hythm exercises\n\n• Partnerwork technique\n\n• Short combinations and
  practical applications\n\nOur goal is to help you understand how to dance
  salsa\, not just memorize steps — developing timing\, connection\, and 
 a comfortable\, joyful way of dancing.\n\nCome dance with us\, grow your t
 echnique\, and experience the energy and flavor of Cuba in a supportive an
 d welcoming environment.\n\nBook your spot\n\nDate & Time:\n\n4week class\
 , November 5- November 26\n\nThursdays @ 7:30 PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood 
 Highway \\#8 San Rafael\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor m
 arking shoe soles allowed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/cuban-salsa/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Dia de Muertos at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T170000
UID:260930v3ShlIJbT0WUSD0KgindGA
DESCRIPTION:In recognition of Día de Muertos\, Jack London State Historic
  Park will present two *ofrendas* in the House of Happy Walls Museum from 
 Oct. 4 to Nov. 6\, 2026.\n\nDia de Muertos\, or Day of the Dead\, is a tra
 dition that began in Mexican and other Latino cultures.  An ofrenda\, Spa
 nish for ‘offering\,’ is an altar created to honor and welcome the mem
 ory of those who have died.\n\nThe Legacy Ofrenda will honor writer and ad
 venturer Jack London\, Charmian London\, and other individuals connected t
 o the history of the property. Through photographs\, reproductions\, tradi
 tional elements of an ofrenda\, and carefully selected symbolic objects\, 
 the installation will reflect Jack and Charmian's partnership\, writing an
 d travels\, their life at Beauty Ranch\, their connection to the land\, an
 d the legacies they left behind.\n\nThe Community Ofrenda will be a shared
 \, participatory offering. Visitors\, locals\, volunteers\, Board members\
 , and employees can contribute a small photograph\, written name\, memory\
 , drawing or message honoring someone who has passed away – including a 
 beloved pet. \n\nThe installation will grow throughout October as more pe
 ople participate.  Materials will be available at the display for visitor
 s who would like to join the celebration and contribute a name\, memory or
  even a drawing of their loved one.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/dia-de-muertos-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mushroom Architect- Chris Maurer- North by North Coast Fall Lectur
 e
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T203000
UID:260925skGtoQVoxkaTq0yVNf9b1w
DESCRIPTION:What if we could grow the materials we build with? Join AIA Re
 dwood Empire for an evening with architect Chris Maurer\, founder of redho
 use studio\, as he explores how mycelium\, the root-like network of mushro
 oms\, can become a building material. From NASA-supported research into sp
 ace habitats to his Mycohab initiative in Namibia\, Maurer’s work offers
  a look at how architecture can turn waste into useful materials and reduc
 e its environmental impact. All are welcome.
LOCATION:Lavish Experience Center
