BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:We Players: Mountain Goddess Ceremony at Western Hills Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261107T180000
UID:2609241MQIiIRU2EivL1rSzDzE3A
DESCRIPTION:Step into the Garden for an immersive ceremony of release\, re
 newal\, and connection to past\, present\, and future.\n\nConceived and di
 rected by Ava Roy and created and performed by Ling Ling Lee\, *Mountain G
 oddess* invites participants into a sensory journey through Western Hills 
 Garden. Guided by the Mountain Goddess and her spirited guardians\, Ox Hea
 d and Horse Face\, guests will move through meditation\, exploration\, rit
 ual\, and play—drawing on ancestry\, memory\, the elements\, and the lan
 dscape itself.\n\nThe experience culminates in a seasonal\, culturally rel
 evant meal prepared by acclaimed Sonoma County Chef Sean Quan\, featuring
  Beijing Zhajiangmian-style noodle bar with an array of different vegetabl
 es\, pickle\, and herb garnishes. Wine\, beer\, non-alcoholic drinks\, and
  cheerful company will also be provided.\n\nPresented by We Players in pa
 rtnership with Western Hills Garden.\n\n**Conceived and Directed by Ava Ro
 y** **Created and Performed by Ling Ling Lee** **Costumes by Brooke Jennin
 gs**\n\nSliding-scale tickets: $100-200 via We Players website.\n\nArtist 
 Bios:\n\n**Ava Roy**: Ava is the Founding Artistic Director of We Players\
 , the Bay Area site-integrated theater company she founded in 2000. For mo
 re than two decades\, she has created immersive performances that bring au
 diences into new relationships with landscape\, history\, and place\, incl
 uding collaborations with the National Park Service\, California State Par
 ks\, and San Francisco Recreation and Parks. Roy is a graduate of Stanford
  University\, where she designed her own major\, Ritual and Performance in
  Aesthetic Education.\n\n**Ling Ling Lee**: Ling Ling is a San Francisco-b
 orn multidisciplinary artist with a background in Chinese theater and danc
 e. A graduate of San Francisco School of the Arts and Shanghai Theatre Aca
 demy\, Lee works across theater\, dance\, storytelling\, and fire performa
 nce. Her collaborators include We Players\, Meow Wolf\, Disney\, Kaimera W
 anderbeasts\, and the European Juggling Convention. With We Players\, Lee 
 has performed as Ox Head/Horse Face in *Psychopomp* and appeared in *Macbe
 th at Fort Point* and *Odyssea*.\n\n**Brooke Jennings**: **Brooke is an aw
 ard-winning costume designer working in the Bay Area and beyond and a grad
 uate of UC Santa Cruz’s Theater Arts master’s program. Her credits inc
 lude work with San Francisco Playhouse\, Shotgun Players\, San Jose Stage\
 , Crowded Fire Theater Company\, and We Players. Jennings began designing 
 for We Players in 2015 with *Ondine at Sutro*\, for which she received a T
 heater Bay Area Award for Outstanding Costume Design\, and has since becom
 e the company’s resident costume designer and a longtime creative collab
 orator.**
LOCATION:Western Hills Garden
URL:https://www.westernhillsgarden.com/programs/we-players-mountain-goddes
 s-2026
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Easy to Love - A Cole Porter Tribute
